<ul data-start=3D"4611" data-end=3D"4788">
<li data-start=3D"4611" data-end=3D"4683" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4613" data-end=3D"4683" class=3D"">Java s=C3=A9pare <stron=
g data-start=3D"4625" data-end=3D"4639">clairement</strong> les classes abs=
traites et les interfaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4684" data-end=3D"4788" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4686" data-end=3D"4788" class=3D"">Une classe peut <strong=
 data-start=3D"4702" data-end=3D"4742">h=C3=A9riter d'une seule classe abst=
raite</strong>, mais <strong data-start=3D"4749" data-end=3D"4785">impl=C3=
=A9menter plusieurs interfaces</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4790" data-end=3D"4793" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4795" data-end=3D"4838" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4798" data-end=3D"4836">5. Bonnes Pratiques en Abstraction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"4840" data-end=3D"4996" class=3D"">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-=
start=3D"4842" data-end=3D"4883">Utiliser une classe abstraite quand :</str=
ong><br data-start=3D"4883" data-end=3D"4886">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F On veut <strong data-start=3D"4897" data-end=3D"4937">fo=
urnir une impl=C3=A9mentation partielle</strong>.<br data-start=3D"4938" da=
ta-end=3D"4941">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Les classes d=C3=A9riv=C3=A9es <strong data-start=3D"496=
5" data-end=3D"4993">partagent du code commun</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4998" data-end=3D"5197" class=3D"">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-=
start=3D"5000" data-end=3D"5034">Utiliser une interface quand :</strong><br=
 data-start=3D"5034" data-end=3D"5037">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F On veut <strong data-start=3D"5048" data-end=3D"5070">im=
poser un contrat</strong> sans d=C3=A9finir de logique interne.<br data-sta=
rt=3D"5103" data-end=3D"5106">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Une classe doit <strong data-start=3D"5125" data-end=3D"=
5163">h=C3=A9riter de plusieurs comportements</strong> (exemple : <code dat=
a-start=3D"5175" data-end=3D"5183">Volant</code>, <code data-start=3D"5185"=
 data-end=3D"5193">Nageur</code>).</p>
<p data-start=3D"5199" data-end=3D"5434" class=3D"">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-=
start=3D"5201" data-end=3D"5257">Privil=C3=A9gier l=E2=80=99abstraction pou=
r r=C3=A9duire la d=C3=A9pendance</strong><br data-start=3D"5257" data-end=
=3D"5260">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Utiliser des <strong data-start=3D"5276" data-end=3D"531=
3">interfaces pour coder par contrat</strong> et non par impl=C3=A9mentatio=
n sp=C3=A9cifique.<br data-start=3D"5351" data-end=3D"5354">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F Favoriser l=E2=80=99<strong data-start=3D"5369" data-end=
=3D"5407">utilisation des classes abstraites</strong> pour structurer le co=
de.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5436" data-end=3D"5439" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5441" data-end=3D"5483" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5444" data-end=3D"5481">6. Abstraction et Design Patterns</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"5485" data-end=3D"5824" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99<strong data-=
start=3D"5487" data-end=3D"5502">abstraction</strong> est au c=C5=93ur de p=
lusieurs <strong data-start=3D"5528" data-end=3D"5547">design patterns</str=
ong> comme :<br data-start=3D"5555" data-end=3D"5558">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F <strong data-start=3D"5561" data-end=3D"5580">Factory Pa=
ttern</strong> (utilise des classes abstraites pour instancier des objets d=
ynamiquement).<br data-start=3D"5655" data-end=3D"5658">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F <strong data-start=3D"5661" data-end=3D"5681">Strategy P=
attern</strong> (remplace un comportement sans modifier le code existant).<=
br data-start=3D"5740" data-end=3D"5743">
=E2=9C=94=EF=B8=8F <strong data-start=3D"5746" data-end=3D"5765">Adapter Pa=
ttern</strong> (facilite la communication entre classes incompatibles).</p>
