<p data-start=3D"4321" data-end=3D"4341" class=3D"">=F0=9F=94=B9 <strong da=
ta-start=3D"4324" data-end=3D"4341">Explication :</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"4342" data-end=3D"4644">
<li data-start=3D"4342" data-end=3D"4536" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4344" data-end=3D"4536" class=3D"">Les m=C3=A9thodes <code=
 data-start=3D"4357" data-end=3D"4367">addition</code> et <code data-start=
=3D"4371" data-end=3D"4385">soustraction</code> sont d=C3=A9finies avec le =
d=C3=A9corateur <code data-start=3D"4419" data-end=3D"4434">@staticmethod</=
code>. Elles ne prennent pas <code data-start=3D"4458" data-end=3D"4464">se=
lf</code> comme argument, car elles ne d=C3=A9pendent pas d'une instance de=
 la classe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4537" data-end=3D"4644" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4539" data-end=3D"4644" class=3D"">Ces m=C3=A9thodes sont =
appel=C3=A9es directement sur la classe, sans avoir besoin de cr=C3=A9er un=
 objet de type <code data-start=3D"4637" data-end=3D"4643">Math</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4646" data-end=3D"4692" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4650" data-end=3D"4692">3.2 Utilisation des M=C3=A9thodes Statiques</strong=
></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4694" data-end=3D"4974" class=3D"">Les m=C3=A9thodes stati=
ques sont utilis=C3=A9es pour des <strong data-start=3D"4741" data-end=3D"4=
783">op=C3=A9rations ind=C3=A9pendantes des instances</strong> de la classe=
. Elles sont utiles lorsque la logique impl=C3=A9ment=C3=A9e ne d=C3=A9pend=
 pas des donn=C3=A9es ou de l'=C3=A9tat d'une instance sp=C3=A9cifique mais=
 est plut=C3=B4t g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rale ou partag=C3=A9e par toutes les instanc=
es.</p>
<p data-start=3D"4976" data-end=3D"5017" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
976" data-end=3D"5017">Cas typiques des m=C3=A9thodes statiques :</strong><=
/p>
<ul data-start=3D"5018" data-end=3D"5368">
<li data-start=3D"5018" data-end=3D"5135" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5020" data-end=3D"5135" class=3D"">Calculs math=C3=A9matiq=
ues, transformations de donn=C3=A9es, ou autres op=C3=A9rations qui ne d=C3=
=A9pendent pas d'un objet sp=C3=A9cifique.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5136" data-end=3D"5257" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5138" data-end=3D"5257" class=3D"">M=C3=A9thodes utilitair=
es ou fonctions de support pour la classe qui ne n=C3=A9cessitent pas d'acc=
=C3=A8s aux attributs de l'instance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5258" data-end=3D"5368" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5260" data-end=3D"5368" class=3D"">Impl=C3=A9mentation de =
la logique de la classe elle-m=C3=AAme sans interagir directement avec des =
objets particuliers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5370" data-end=3D"5373" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5375" data-end=3D"5449" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5378" data-end=3D"5449">4. Diff=C3=A9rences Cl=C3=A9s entre M=C3=A9thodes d=
'Instance et M=C3=A9thodes Statiques</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5451" data-end=3D"5480" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5455" data-end=3D"5480">4.1 Acc=C3=A8s aux Donn=C3=A9es</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5481" data-end=3D"5784">
<li data-start=3D"5481" data-end=3D"5594" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5483" data-end=3D"5594" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
483" data-end=3D"5505">M=C3=A9thode d'instance</strong> : Elle acc=C3=A8de =
=C3=A0 des <strong data-start=3D"5526" data-end=3D"5550">attributs d'instan=
ce</strong> sp=C3=A9cifiques =C3=A0 chaque objet, gr=C3=A2ce =C3=A0 <code d=
ata-start=3D"5587" data-end=3D"5593">self</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5595" data-end=3D"5784" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5597" data-end=3D"5784" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
597" data-end=3D"5617">M=C3=A9thode statique</strong> : Elle ne peut pas ac=
c=C3=A9der aux <strong data-start=3D"5649" data-end=3D"5673">attributs d'in=
stance</strong> ou =C3=A0 <code data-start=3D"5679" data-end=3D"5685">self<=
/code>, car elle ne d=C3=A9pend pas d'une instance. Elle travaille sur les =
<strong data-start=3D"5749" data-end=3D"5763">param=C3=A8tres</strong> pass=
=C3=A9s =C3=A0 la m=C3=A9thode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5786" data-end=3D"5809" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5790" data-end=3D"5809">4.2 Utilisation</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5810" data-end=3D"6015">
<li data-start=3D"5810" data-end=3D"5910" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5812" data-end=3D"5910" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
812" data-end=3D"5834">M=C3=A9thode d'instance</strong> : Elle n=C3=A9cessi=
te la cr=C3=A9ation d'une instance de la classe pour =C3=AAtre appel=C3=A9e=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5911" data-end=3D"6015" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5913" data-end=3D"6015" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
913" data-end=3D"5933">M=C3=A9thode statique</strong> : Elle peut =C3=AAtre=
 appel=C3=A9e directement sur la <strong data-start=3D"5978" data-end=3D"59=
88">classe</strong>, sans cr=C3=A9ation d'instance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6017" data-end=3D"6039" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
