</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4434" data-end=3D"4522" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4438" data-end=3D"4522">3.2 R=C3=A9solution du Probl=C3=A8me du Diamant : L=
a m=C3=A9thode MRO (Method Resolution Order)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4524" data-end=3D"4777" class=3D"">Les langages modernes q=
ui supportent l'h=C3=A9ritage multiple, comme <strong data-start=3D"4588" d=
ata-end=3D"4598">Python</strong>, r=C3=A9solvent ce probl=C3=A8me avec une =
approche appel=C3=A9e <strong data-start=3D"4648" data-end=3D"4681">MRO (Me=
thod Resolution Order)</strong>. Cette technique d=C3=A9finit l'ordre dans =
lequel les m=C3=A9thodes et attributs sont h=C3=A9rit=C3=A9s et r=C3=A9solu=
s.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4779" data-end=3D"4814" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4784" data-end=3D"4814">Exemple de MRO en Python :</strong></h4>
<pre class=3D"overflow-visible!" data-start=3D"4816" data-end=3D"5240"><div=
