=C3=A9thode <code data-start=3D"7048" data-end=3D"7063">calcul_area()</code=
>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7065" data-end=3D"7291" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7067" data-end=3D"7291" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
067" data-end=3D"7084">Extensibilit=C3=A9</strong> : Si de nouvelles formes=
 doivent =C3=AAtre ajout=C3=A9es (par exemple, <strong data-start=3D"7146" =
data-end=3D"7158">Triangle</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"7160" data-end=
=3D"7169">Carr=C3=A9</strong>, etc.), vous pouvez simplement cr=C3=A9er une=
 nouvelle classe qui h=C3=A9rite de <strong data-start=3D"7241" data-end=3D=
"7250">Forme</strong> et red=C3=A9finir la m=C3=A9thode <code data-start=3D=
"7275" data-end=3D"7290">calcul_area()</code>.</p>
